<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grenoble</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grenoble is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, at the meeting of the Isère and Drac rivers among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. It was the capital of the Dauphiné, whose ruler Humbert II founded its university in 1339, and it was the seat of a parlement. The 'Day of the Tiles' riot there in 1788 is seen as an early sign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. It hosted the Winter Olympic Games in 1968.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grenoble.jpg" alt="Grenoble" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simdaperce · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_grenoble.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
